# Contains the RDS master password. Never commit.
.env
infra/stack.json

# FloodNet data is under a noncommercial license. Do not redistribute it via a
# public repo: cache it locally, ingest it, never commit it.
#
# The allowlist below is the safe direction (deny by default) and it has a cost
# worth knowing: a NEW fixture is silently ignored, `git add` reports nothing,
# and the file exists on your disk and nowhere else. That happened to
# replay.escalation.json, which was written, tested against, referenced by the
# run book, and never committed. See E-031. Add an exception here whenever you
# add a fixture, and TestEscalationFixture asserts the tracking so the mistake
# cannot survive a test run.
data/*.json
!data/replay.example.json
!data/replay.escalation.json
# 162 KB, well under the size at which a fixture stops belonging in git. Built
# from recorded FloodNet readings by data/convert_floodnet.py. The 4.7 MB raw
# NYC Open Data download it derives from is deliberately NOT committed.
!data/replay.floodnet.json

.venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
screenshots/raw/

# EC2 login key. Publishing it hands anyone ubuntu on the instance, and deleting
# the commit afterward is not a fix: the pair has to be rotated and the box
# relaunched.
*.pem

# Consolidation archive from the v0.4.1 import. The tree supersedes it.
files.zip
